{"units": [{"id": "eurymachos-def1", "translation": "Eurymachus fr. 178. He is one of the suitors of Penelope, known from Homer's Odyssey."}, {"id": "euruporos-orth1", "translation": "having broad or wide passages"}, {"id": "euruporos-def1", "translation": "having broad or wide passages"}, {"id": "euruporos-quote1", "translation": "of the wide-pathed sea"}, {"id": "eurus-orth1", "translation": "wide, broad"}, {"id": "eurus-def1", "translation": "wide, broad"}, {"id": "eurus-note1", "translation": "The reading is corrupt. Hermann: Ἀερίαισιν [with airy] (Hartung: Ἀερίαις ἐν [in airy]) αὔραις [breezes]."}, {"id": "eurus-quote1", "translation": "in wide breezes"}, {"id": "eurus-word1", "translation": "Ἀερίαισιν [with airy] (Ἀερίαις ἐν [in airy]"}, {"id": "eurus-word2", "translation": "αὔραις [breezes]"}, {"id": "europa-orth1", "translation": "Europa"}, {"id": "europa-def1", "translation": "Europa"}, {"id": "europa-def2", "translation": "The play of Aeschylus was entitled Κᾶρες ἢ Εὐρώπη [Carians or Europa] (fr. 98 99)"}, {"id": "europa-quote1", "translation": "leaving the land of Europa"}, {"id": "europa-quote2", "translation": "from Europa"}, {"id": "europa-quote3", "translation": "of the land of Europa"}, {"id": "europa-word1", "translation": "Κᾶρες ἢ Εὐρώπη [Carians or Europa]"}, {"id": "eusebeia-orth1", "translation": "piety"}, {"id": "eusebeia-def1", "translation": "piety"}, {"id": "eusebeia-quote1", "translation": "Ares defiling piety"}, {"id": "eusebeo-orth1", "translation": "to worship piously"}, {"id": "eusebeo-def1", "translation": "to worship piously"}, {"id": "eusebeo-quote1", "translation": "if they worship piously the gods who protect the city"}, {"id": "eusebeo-quote2", "translation": "you are dishonored throughout the city of the pious"}, {"id": "eusebes-orth1", "translation": "pious"}, {"id": "eusebes-def1", "translation": "pious"}, {"id": "eusebes-note1", "translation": "where the added καλλίων [more beautiful] Dobraeus changed to κλαίων [weeping], whence Hermann: μηρών τε τῶν σῶν εὐσέβησ᾽ ὁμιλίαν | κλάων [weeping, I revered the company of your thighs]."}, {"id": "eusebes-quote1", "translation": "a pious man"}, {"id": "eusebes-quote2", "translation": "but the impious one"}, {"id": "eusebes-quote3", "translation": "how then am I pious in your eyes?"}, {"id": "eusebes-quote4", "translation": "a pious protector"}, {"id": "eusebes-quote5", "translation": "if a pious word should persuade"}, {"id": "eusebes-quote6", "translation": "the pious company of your thighs"}, {"id": "eusebes-quote7", "translation": "and these things are pious for me from the gods"}, {"id": "eusebes-quote8", "translation": "to become much more chaste than my mother and more pious in hand"}, {"id": "eusebes-word1", "translation": "καλλίων [more beautiful]"}, {"id": "eusebes-word2", "translation": "κλαίων [weeping]"}, {"id": "eusebes-word3", "translation": "μηρών τε τῶν σῶν εὐσέβησ᾽ ὁμιλίαν | κλάων [weeping, I revered the company of your thighs]"}, {"id": "eusemos-orth1", "translation": "conspicuous, notable"}, {"id": "eusemos-def1", "translation": "conspicuous, notable"}, {"id": "eusemos-quote1", "translation": "the city, taken by smoke, is still conspicuous"}, {"id": "eusemos-quote2", "translation": "for it does not escape my notice, being conspicuous"}, {"id": "euskopos-orth1", "translation": "aiming well"}, {"id": "euskopos-def1", "translation": "aiming well"}, {"id": "euskopos-quote1", "translation": "being subdued from afar by well-aimed arrows"}, {"id": "eustales-orth1", "translation": "equipped, ready"}, {"id": "eustales-def1", "translation": "equipped, ready"}, {"id": "eustales-quote1", "translation": "we shall raise a well-equipped chosen expedition"}, {"id": "eustomew-orth1", "translation": "to speak well or correctly"}, {"id": "eustomew-def1", "translation": "to speak well or correctly"}, {"id": "eustomew-quote1", "translation": "even if I happen to speak very well"}, {"id": "eutaktos-orth1", "translation": "well-ordered"}, {"id": "eutaktos-def1", "translation": "well-ordered"}, {"id": "eutaktos-quote1", "translation": "first the right wing, well-ordered"}, {"id": "eute-orth1", "translation": "when"}, {"id": "eute-def1", "translation": "when"}, {"id": "eute-note1", "translation": "With the indicative"}, {"id": "eute-note2", "translation": "At the beginning of a defective verse. Hermann supplied εὐτέ γε [when at least]."}, {"id": "eute-note3", "translation": "With the optative"}, {"id": "eute-note4", "translation": "εὐτ᾽ ἄν [whenever] with the subjunctive"}, {"id": "eute-note5", "translation": "thus Scholefield for ὁρᾶν [to see]"}, {"id": "eute-note6", "translation": "Without ἄν"}, {"id": "eute-quote1", "translation": "when Laius begot death for himself"}, {"id": "eute-quote2", "translation": "when the aged Darius, equal to a god, ruled the land"}, {"id": "eute-quote3", "translation": "when the Achaean host was weighed down by empty distress of the sea"}, {"id": "eute-quote4", "translation": "when the sailor army set out against Ilium"}, {"id": "eute-quote5", "translation": "when the sea in its midday resting places sleeps calm and windless"}, {"id": "eute-quote6", "translation": "whenever we come into the house"}, {"id": "eute-quote7", "translation": "whenever the sun, blazing with rays, ceases to scorch the earth"}, {"id": "eute-quote8", "translation": "whenever I have a night-wandering and dewy bed"}, {"id": "eute-quote9", "translation": "whenever he learns the word"}, {"id": "eute-quote10", "translation": "whenever someone, thinking good things, sees"}, {"id": "eute-quote11", "translation": "when the city is subdued"}, {"id": "eute-word1", "translation": "εὐτέ γε [when at least]"}, {"id": "eute-word2", "translation": "εὐτ᾽ ἄν [whenever]"}, {"id": "eute-word3", "translation": "ὁρᾶν [to see]"}, {"id": "eute-word4", "translation": "ἄ [which]"}, {"id": "euteknos-orth1", "translation": "blessed with offspring"}, {"id": "euteknos-def1", "translation": "blessed with offspring"}, {"id": "euteknos-quote1", "translation": "the seed of a cow blessed with offspring"}, {"id": "euteles-orth1", "translation": "cheap, worthless"}, {"id": "euteles-def1", "translation": "cheap, worthless"}, {"id": "euteles-quote1", "translation": "the maker of signs was not a worthless man"}, {"id": "eutlemon-orth1", "translation": "steadfast, enduring"}, {"id": "eutlemon-def1", "translation": "steadfast, enduring"}, {"id": "eutlemon-note1", "translation": "Thus from some copies for ἐντλήμονι [in the steadfast], as M, or ἐν τλήμονι [in the steadfast], as other copies. The word is not read elsewhere: for no weight should be given to Hermann's conjecture on Eur. Med. 865,"}, {"id": "eutlemon-quote1", "translation": "with a steadfast soul"}, {"id": "eutlemon-word1", "translation": "ἐντλήμονι [in the steadfast]"}, {"id": "eutlemon-word2", "translation": "ἐν τλήμονι [in the steadfast]"}, {"id": "eutolmos-orth1", "translation": "bold"}, {"id": "eutolmos-def1", "translation": "bold"}, {"id": "eutolmos-def2", "translation": "boldly"}, {"id": "eutolmos-quote1", "translation": "from a bold heart"}, {"id": "eutolmos-quote2", "translation": "you tread boldly to the altar"}, {"id": "eutrapeZos-orth1", "translation": "furnished with a good table"}, {"id": "eutrapeZos-def1", "translation": "furnished with a good table"}, {"id": "eutrapeZos-quote1", "translation": "through the well-furnished halls of my father"}, {"id": "eutraphes-orth1", "translation": "well-nourishing"}, {"id": "eutraphes-def1", "translation": "well-nourishing"}, {"id": "eutraphes-note1", "translation": "Thus from the copy for εὐτρεφέστατον [most well-nourishing]."}, {"id": "eutraphes-quote1", "translation": "you milked well-nourishing milk"}, {"id": "eutraphes-quote2", "translation": "and Dircean water, most well-nourishing of drinks"}, {"id": "eutraphes-word1", "translation": "εὐτρεφέστατον [most well-nourishing]"}, {"id": "eutrepes-orth1", "translation": "Sept. 89 faulty reading. See λευκοπρεπής."}, {"id": "eutrepes-def1", "translation": "Sept. 89 faulty reading. See λευκοπρεπής."}, {"id": "eutrepes-word1", "translation": "λευκοπρεπής [white-looking]"}, {"id": "eutrepizo-orth1", "translation": "to have ready"}, {"id": "eutrepizo-def1", "translation": "to have ready"}, {"id": "eutrepizo-quote1", "translation": "let everyone make ready a sword with hilt forward"}, {"id": "eutrephes_see_eutraphes-orth1", "translation": "See εὐτραφής."}, {"id": "eutrephes_see_eutraphes-def1", "translation": "See εὐτραφής."}, {"id": "eutrephes_see_eutraphes-word1", "translation": "εὐτραφής [well-nourishing]"}]}